iver and i think to get a first  round pick for him at a time when you  are clearly rebuilding makes a ton of  sense it's just another potentially  talented player that the raiders will  take into las vegas they have three  first-round picks now in 2019 and  clearly they have given up on this  season and i was i don't know is it  stunning i was i'd like to get your  reaction i was somewhere between  surprised and stunned that the players  weren't told about the trade by john  gruden himself that they found out on  their phones and then he won't even  address them about the trade until  wednesday it seems like you could plan  it out a little bit better so the coach  can break the news to the players and at  least get a talking point or two out  there that you hope that maybe the  players will repeat when when being  questioned by reporters  well i think the problem there is you're  coming off your bye week and  there's  there's really not any way in my opinion  anyway that they could have done it any  differently for a very simple reason you  know the cowboys aren't going to keep  this under wraps for  x number of hours i mean the only way  you could have done something is if you  sent a mass text a group text to your  players and explain to them why you did  this  but then somebody's going to leak the  text to the press and you know i don't  know i don't think they really could  have done it any differently i do think  this going forward look the dallas  cowboys clearly have not  have said that  we want to give our young quarterback  every chance there's nobody that's very  good in this division this year we just  got officiated maybe out of an overtime  and maybe a win in washington  uh with the bad call in my opinion a  horrendous call  at the end of regulation you know on the  uh on the snap penalty you know on the  long snapper and the cowboys have to be  thinking that we can win this division  so we are all in this year hey good for  them i think they overpaid 