d you're  putting him in a position now where  everybody is going to expect him to be  julio jones jr  if you're getting traded for a one and  you're coming in to be the number one  receiver on america's team the focus is  going to be uber  over what it was in oakland and in  oakland they already were trying to get  him the ball all the time so there is  the the problem that you're talking  about mike  but and i'd love to know and maybe we'll  find out in time some of the inner  discussions that happened with the  cowboys as to whether or not to go  through with this it was very curious  that jerry jones avoided reporters after  the game on sunday out of character for  jones to have nothing to say he had  cancelled his tuesday appearance on  105.3 the fan in dallas in advance of  the trade and now the trade's done it'd  be interesting to see if he goes ahead  and goes through with it unless there's  something else he's trying to keep under  wraps but i i just i can't imagine that  everyone was on the same page that it  makes sense to give up a first-round  pick for a guy who may not be a number  one receiver and this is going to  complicate jason garrett's life going  forward as he tries to coach this team  let's keep talking about this amari  cooper trade from the raiders to the  cowboys we've got plenty more pft live  to come and i want to look at it also  from the financial angle because amari  cooper's got a 13.9 million dollar  salary for next year and when it's time  to sign into a contract it can get very  expensive hi i'm mike tarico and thanks  for watching make sure to hit subscribe  for the latest news and highlights from  nbc sports

